Z||000003||fiero56||10-02-2001||12:09 AM||||Goto <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>www.suspension.com</A> <P>They have part#s. Prothane is the only manufacturer of poly for Fiero.<P>I called NOPI once. First guy didn't speak english("what country do you think this is" - from Ferris), I was handed off to the "English" speaking guy to whom I had to spell out the letters  P-O-N-T-I-A-C and F-I-E-R-O(remember now, I had the part#s in front of me). The guy never did understand what I was saying, and ended up saying he didn't think they sold polyurethane bushings at all. After that I bought my bushings from suspension.com . <P>A buddy of mine has ordered 3 times over the last year from NOPI, and has never received an order to NOPI yet(he has given them part #s too). But, there are a few on here who have had better results than us, but I will never call them again.<P>When I call a business...I'm not even going to finish. It would make me feel safer when it at least sounded like I was dealing with someone with an education higher than 3rd grade...<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-02-2001).]||||reg||1
